{
  "seed_edits": [],
  "bindings": {
    "admin_robert_walsh": ["U03ROBERT23"],
    "general_channel": ["C01ABCD1234"],
    "random_channel": ["C02EFGH5678"],
    "engineering_channel": ["C03IJKL9012"],
    "growth_channel": ["C04MNOP3456"],
    "project_alpha_channel": ["C05ALPHA"],
    "project_alpha_dev_channel": ["C06ALPHADEV"],
    "core_infra_channel": ["C_INFRA"],
    "admin_morgan_freeman": ["U07MORGANFREE"],
    "actor": ["U01AGENBOT9"]
  },
  "selectors": [
    {
      "root_table": "channels",
      "scope": [
        {"field": "team_id", "op": "eq", "value": "T01WORKSPACE"}
      ],
      "focal": {
        "path": ["channels", "channel_members", "users", "user_teams"],
        "joins": ["channel_members.channel_id", "channel_members.user_id", "user_teams.user_id"],
        "filters": [
          {"node": 3, "field": "team_id", "op": "eq", "value": "T01WORKSPACE"},
          {"node": 3, "field": "role", "op": "eq", "value": "admin"}
        ]
      },
      "auxiliary": []
    }
  ],
  "negative_referents": ["C04MNOP3456", "C05ALPHA", "C06ALPHADEV", "C_INFRA"],
  "notes": "Actor binding corrected to U01AGENBOT9 to match case.acting_user_id. U01AGENBOT9 already holds a T01WORKSPACE membership (user_teams) and is itself a member of general, random, and engineering (per base channel_members), so it retains a real anchor into the qualifying channels in addition to relying on unrestricted team-wide discovery endpoints (conversations.list, users.list, conversations.members) for the remaining public channels. No other seed changes were needed: base seed already contains U03ROBERT23 (Robert Walsh, admin, member of general/random/engineering) and U07MORGANFREE (Morgan Freeman, admin, no channel memberships), plus negatives growth (all-member roles), project-alpha (single bot member), project-alpha-dev and core-infra (contain a same-named non-admin 'Robert Chen'). Selector scope restricts to T01WORKSPACE (a legitimate stated scope field, not an answer-restricting shortcut); the focal query finds channels whose membership includes any user holding the workspace-admin role, yielding general, random, and engineering as the qualifying set, with Robert Walsh as the admin member in each."
}
